Yes, the two levers are easy to locate and identify. The one on top is
black. The other one is brass (color).
The RA82 uses the same procedure BTW.
I've heard many people complain about the RA8x drives. Actually they weren't
all that bad, provided they were
kept powered on. That way they lasted 5 years and more. Heavy, yes,
unreliable, not with the ones I worked with
(more than 40), but I wouldn't call them fast. Well, the UDA50 wasn't that
fast either, let alone an 11/750...

The TU80 is a device of which I'm glad its details are gone from my memory.
A ....slow.... 1600 bpi drive that was
difficult to keep it in streaming mode, even on an 8550. Anyway, IIRC there
was a locking nut that went into the
face plate that also held the reels. The top horizontal surface.
Then again, it's too long ago so my memory is probably wrong.

Hans




